### Short plain-English legend (one-line per underbrace)
- inertia — mass-like resistance of filament nodes and membrane modes to acceleration.  
- damping — viscous or internal dissipation acting on velocities.  
- stiffness — nominal linear restoring tendencies (bending, membrane tension).  
- \(\mathbf{F}_{\text{contact}}\) — direct contact/twine: normal repulsion, dashpot, friction.  
- \(\mathbf{F}_{\text{mem}\leftarrow\text{fil}\right.}\) — membrane reaction tractions sampled at filament nodes.  
- \(\mathbf{F}_{\text{fil}\to\text{mem}}\) — filament nodal forces regularized and projected into membrane modal forcing.  
- \(\mathbf{F}_{\text{hydro}}\) — hydrodynamic coupling via a mobility operator (long-range fluid-mediated interactions).  
- \(\mathbf{\Lambda}\) — constraint forces enforcing inextensibility / non-penetration (Lagrange multipliers or penalty terms).  
- \(\Delta\mathbf{K}\) — nonlinear elastic corrections capturing parasitic radial vibrations and geometry-dependent stiffness.  
- \(\mathbf{F}_{\text{ext}}\) — any external drive / control inputs.

